From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:55:47 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 14/42] hw/audio: Add the i.MX21 SSI and audio multiplexer

The stock Chumby kernel's TSC2100 driver plays and records through
SSI1: it routes SSI1 through the AUDMUX to the codec's pins (receive
data from peripheral port 1, transmit data out on ports 1 and 2), runs
SSI1 as an I2S slave in network mode with four 16-bit slots per frame,
two of them unmasked, and moves the data with the DMA controller on
SSI1's FIFO 0 requests (transmit watermark 4, receive watermark 6).

Model SSI1 and SSI2 as slaves of whatever codec sits behind the AUDMUX:
their FIFOs, watermark and status flags, underrun and overrun, the
interrupt and the four DMA requests, normal, network and two-channel
modes, word lengths and bit 0 or bit 31 alignment, and the slot masks.
A codec clocks frames out of and into the SSI as 16-bit stereo through
imx21_audmux_transmit() and imx21_audmux_receive(), which follow the
AUDMUX's data routing. The SSI's clock generator, frame sync flags,
AC97 mode and the AUDMUX's clock routing are not modelled.

Wire both to the SoC with their interrupts and DMA request lines.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
